# Daily Docker hygiene — 04:30 prod daemon (after Watchtower's 04:00 sweep has pulled the new
# images, so the superseded ones are unused by then), 04:35 the Actions runners' rootless
# daemon, 04:40 the runners' self-update leftovers. Per-directory bounds: docs/disk.md.
#
# Prod daemon (images live in /var/lib/containerd — the containerd image store):
# - Images no container uses and older than 48h. Weekly was too slow: 7.6 GB of superseded
#   RollHook tags and factory step images piled up in the 2.4 days after the Sunday run
#   (measured 2026-11-17, issue_2033); the 48h window keeps this week's rollback targets and
#   the factory's fresh step image warm.
# - Build cache capped at 3 GB (least recently used goes first), so RollHook's layer cache
#   stays warm. `builder prune` WITHOUT `-a` removes only dangling records, and on this
#   engine (29.x, containerd store) `--filter until=` matches nothing at all — a daily
#   `until=48h` run reclaimed 0 B while 18 GB of 4-week-old cache sat there. Size caps work.
# NEVER volumes — that is data (Postgres, ClickHouse, RollHook, fpp-analytics).
# Stopped containers are left alone too: RollHook's rollout leaves none, and a stopped one is
# evidence worth reading before it goes.
# The log gets the totals only (the per-image `deleted:` lines were 57 KB of noise).
# Install: make prune-cron-install   (copies to /etc/cron.d, or setup.sh section 12)
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin

30 4 * * * jkrumm /bin/bash -c 'echo "=== $(date -u +\%FT\%TZ)"; docker image prune -af --filter until=48h | tail -n 1; docker builder prune -af --max-used-space 3GB | tail -n 1; docker system df' >> /home/jkrumm/docker-prune.log 2>&1
# Same for the Actions runners' rootless daemon (docs/gh-runner.md) — every CI and deploy build
# lands there. Volumes too, unlike above: on this daemon they are only what jobs' service
# containers left behind, never data. A no-op until `make gh-runner-setup` has created the user.
# DAILY, and the cache capped by SIZE (6 GB): CI churn is ~40 GB/week (images, job volumes, build
# cache), a weekly sweep let the 178 GB disk cross 90% on 2026-11-17 (incident issue_1842), and
# the daily sweep that followed still left 18 GB of cache because its `--filter until=48h` matches
# nothing here (see above). 6 GB holds weatherorb's 3 GB core-ci image layers plus the other
# repos' builds; images and volumes go every day, so the day's peak is churn + 6 GB.
35 4 * * * gh-runner /bin/bash -c 'export DOCKER_HOST=unix:///run/user/$(id -u)/docker.sock; echo "=== $(date -u +\%FT\%TZ)"; docker image prune -af | tail -n 1; docker builder prune -af --max-used-space 6GB | tail -n 1; docker volume prune -af | tail -n 1; docker system df' >> /home/gh-runner/docker-prune.log 2>&1
# Runners' self-update leftovers: old bin/externals and _work/_update (~8 GB measured), as root
# because the repo is not readable by gh-runner. It also trims host scratch (stale ~/exp<issue>
# dirs, /tmp pytest leftovers, the apt cache). scripts/gh-runner-clean.sh explains the guards.
40 4 * * * root /home/jkrumm/vps/scripts/gh-runner-clean.sh >> /var/log/gh-runner-clean.log 2>&1
